<mujoco model="IST_robot">
  <!--
Load this file for MuJoCo physics; the companion URDF alone lacks yoke closure.
One actuator: motor_velocity, ctrl in rad/s of the input shaft. Start at 0,
then ramp towards e.g. 100 to 500 rad/s. Ctrl limit +/-2000 rad/s and torque
limit +/-0.002 Nm are provisional, not a characterized motor model.
Exact ideal ratios and pin-in-slot geometry; no gear tooth contact, backlash,
frictional efficiency or elastic tooth deformation. Pin follower is a virtual
1 nanogram solver body. The yoke is closed with a connect constraint, NOT a
polynomial approximation to sin. Rack-pinion pitch radius = 0.00195 m.
Feathering is passive: no actuator/mimic/sinusoidal prescription. User confirmed
+/-26.1 degree mechanical stops, no torsion spring or elastic return; stiffness=0.
Joint damping 1e-8 Nms/rad is provisional. Air is approximated by
MuJoCo ellipsoid fluid forces; coefficients are illustrative, not calibrated.
Material inertials: solid CNC PEEK mechanisms, PET wing frames, 10 um Kapton films.
See ../materials.json and ../recalculate_inertials.py; base_link is unchanged.
Original CAD density 1000 kg/m3 is inferred from mesh volumes, not measured.
The motor STEP merges stator/rotor; separate rotor
inertia is unknown and is not invented. Base is fixed as in the bench assembly.
Membrane mass is integrated once; reverse visual faces add no extra mass.
All STL geoms are visual; mesh contacts are disabled because convex hulls would
fill the rings/slots. This model is not validated for impacts or lift prediction.
Keys: home (zero speed), run_100 (100 rad/s), run_500 (500 rad/s).
-->
